`analyze` prints a query file's diagnostics as a JSON array (analyze.in/):
an unknown KQL operator is an error at its range; a clean SPL search has none.

```console
$ opentide-lsp analyze broken.kql
[
  {
    "code": "kql_unknown_operator",
    "severity": "error",
    "message": "unknown tabular operator 'frobnicate'",
    "range": {
      "start": {
        "line": 2,
        "character": 2
      },
      "end": {
        "line": 2,
        "character": 12
      }
    }
  }
]

$ opentide-lsp analyze clean.spl
[]

```
